2027-01-04T16:27:35  message   To the owner:
For 3 days in [ADDRESS] with no crowds - March is actually a good pick, it's shoulder season:

Day 1 - oldest neighborhoods, early and on foot. Start super early in Alfama / Graca / Mouraria for viewpoints and just wandering, then duck into a couple small museums or churches midday when tour groups are out. Evening fado in a tiny spot rather than the big dinner halls.

Day 2 - Belem without the bus crowds. Go on a weekday, first thing for one big sight and then walk further west to Ajuda / Alcantara / LX Factory area, which is much calmer. Riverfront walks are best late afternoon.

Day 3 - get out of center. Either Sintra at opening on a weekday with pre-booked timed tickets, or skip Sintra entirely for the south bank / Arrabida coast or Monsanto park if you want nature and space.

General crowd-avoidance that works well there: stay west of Baixa or in Graca instead of right in Alfama/Baixa, book timed tickets ahead, do big sights at opening or last hour, and walk between close neighborhoods instead of the packed trams/tuk-tuks midday.

Want me to shape this around your March 12-19 dates - like which 3 days, what pace you like, and budget?

P.S. I still have your 3 saves in my active notes - [ADDRESS] dates, no messages before 10am unless on fire, and The Overstory back to [PERSON_NAME] by end of Jan. My file tools are still returning garbled text instead of saving, so I'm keeping them here until that clears up.

